{"id": "EUVD-2026-107500", "enisaUuid": "58d820bb-8c9a-38d0-ad7d-d772cc7e91b9", "description": "Apache Traffic Server can resume a TLS session across SNI virtual hosts without re-verifying a client certificate required by the resumed host's verify_client STRICT policy.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Traffic Server: from 8.0.0 through 8.1.11, from 9.0.0 through 9.2.15, from 10.0.0 through 10.1.4, 10.2.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.2.16, 10.1.5, or 10.2.1, which fix the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T19:13:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:06:21", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/r95dq29ywcd1f4x30snxlqmb12z4s4kc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111815", "GHSA-h35r-68fc-8f5m"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "78f85121-f0ef-30f0-b6f3-1aa1d343cabd", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.0.0 \u226410.1.4"}, {"id": "e5addb94-a897-3781-b95e-aa4c1e546a5f", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0 \u22648.1.11"}, {"id": "f2a6eada-5614-30e0-9460-08fe1d640fbe", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0 \u22649.2.15"}, {"id": "fb32f4f0-737c-387e-b5df-67fc8d044b84", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e6f40dce-9cd9-372f-a47f-c009a6eb5cf4", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}